1. ENFORCE CANONICAL TIP CONTINUITY
===================================

ApplyBlock currently only compares block.Height with the checkpoint height.

That is not sufficient.

A canonical state mutation must be serialized around sync_state('main') and
the incoming block must have an explicit relationship to the current tip.

At the start of ApplyBlock, inside its pgx transaction:

  SELECT indexed_height, indexed_block_hash
  FROM sync_state
  WHERE name='main'
  FOR UPDATE

This row lock is the canonical-chain mutation lock and must also be acquired
by RollbackTo before it changes canonical state.

For an initialized store, ApplyBlock should accept exactly:

A. exact current-tip replay:

   block.Hash == checkpoint.Hash
   block.Height == checkpoint.Height

or

B. immediate canonical append:

   block.Height == checkpoint.Height + 1
   block.PreviousHash == checkpoint.Hash

Anything else should return a new sentinel such as:

  ErrNonSequentialBlock

and MUST leave the database unchanged.

Do not allow a lower historical block to mutate canonical UTXO/address
state merely because its height is below the checkpoint.

For an uninitialized checkpoint (-1/NULL), preserve whatever intentional
bootstrap policy is needed for the existing isolated fixture tests, but
document it explicitly. Production historical sync will start from genesis.

